# Lesson 5, new exercise: after 2♥, responder invites with five spades; opener declines.
title: Five spades, partner declines
id: L05-19
type: exercise
lesson: 5
concepts: 5.4
student: S
board: 40
dealer: W
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KJ     AJ75   JT5    AQ43
  E  T7     K843   A97    K875
  S  Q9864  92     KQ84   J2
  W  A532   QT6    632    T96

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 15-17 points, balanced
  E Pass
  S 2C*    = Stayman: do you have a 4-card major?
     key: 8 points and five spades: start with Stayman.
     not 2S: 2♠ now would be weak, under 8 points. You have 8.
  W Pass
  N 2H     = Four hearts
  E Pass
  S 2S*    = Five spades, 8-9 points, not four hearts
     key: No heart fit. 2♠ shows five spades and invites.
     not 2NT: 2NT would show only four spades. Show your fifth.
     not 3S: 3♠ would show 10+ points. You have 8.
  W Pass
  N 2NT    = A minimum, only two spades
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Accept partner's decision
     key: Partner has a minimum and no spade fit. Stop here.
     not 3S: Partner has denied three spades. 2NT is fine.
     not 3NT: Partner declined your invitation. Respect it.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You showed five spades and an invitation. Partner had only two spades and 16
  points, near the bottom of the range, so she declined with 2NT. North is
  declarer, because North bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the
  first trick.

play:
  1   E C5  S CJ  W C6  N C3
  2   S SQ  W S2  N SJ  E S7
      note: Dummy's spades are the long suit to set up.
  3   S S9  W S3  N SK  E ST
      note: Declarer plays the ♠K so dummy's spades can run later.
  4   N DJ  E D7  S DQ  W D2
      note: Lead the ♦J to reach dummy's diamonds.
  5   S S8  W S5  N C4  E H3
      note: Keep leading spades to knock out the ace.
  6   S S6  W SA  N H5  E H4
      note: Drive out the ♠A.
  7   W D6  N D5  E D9  S DK
  8   S S4  W D3  N H7  E C7
      note: The spades are set up.
  9   S D8  W H6  N DT  E DA
      note: Lead a diamond toward declarer.
  10  E HK  S H2  W HT  N HA
  11  N CA  E C8  S C2  W C9
      note: Cash the club winner.
  12  N HJ  E H8  S H9  W HQ
      note: Exit with a heart.
  13  W CT  N CQ  E CK  S D4
      note: 9 tricks: 2NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♠A to set up dummy's long spades, keeping a
  way to reach them.

  2NT made nine tricks, so 3NT would have made too. Partner's decision was
  still sound: with 16 points and no spade fit, game needed things to go
  well, and this time they did. Good bidding doesn't always reach the best
  score.
